# Whole .vscode dir: c_cpp_properties.json carries absolute include paths that
# expose the local username. Deliberately excluded when this repo was rebuilt
# public on 2026-09-20; without this rule a `git add -A` puts them straight back.
.vscode/
**/.vscode/

# --- credentials: ignore by NAME anywhere, not just at the two paths above ---
# The path-specific rules alone did not cover backups or editor swap files, all of
# which hold the same plaintext. Found 2026-08-04 with four such files untracked and
# sweepable by `git add -A` -- in a repo that has already leaked this PSK once.
# (This repo is PRIVATE as of 2026-08-09; it was public when that leak happened. Note
# that GitHub push protection is NOT available on private repos without paid Secret
# Protection, so this file is the only thing standing between a stray `git add -A` and
# a committed credential. Keep it name-based.)
arduino_secrets.h
arduino_secrets.h.*
*secrets*.h
*secrets*.h.*

# editor swap/backup files -- a .swp of a secrets file contains the secrets
*.swp
*.swo
.*.swp
.*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.bak-*

# compiled firmware -- the PSK and OTA password are baked into the binary in
# cleartext, so a .bin is a credential file even though it does not look like one.
# `git add -f` if one ever genuinely needs to be committed.
*.bin
secrets.yaml
